<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Foraged food (RimWorld: RawBerries in ThingDefs_Items/Items_Food).

    Its own file rather than an entry in Items_Food.xml, per CLAUDE.md: DefLoader.AddDirectory reads every
    XML file under a Def folder, so additive content never needs an edit to a shared one.

    WHY THIS DEF EXISTS AT ALL. Before it, a generated map carried no nutrition whatsoever. Map generation
    scattered WildPlant, which has no harvestedThingDef and no ingestible block; nothing else on an interior
    was edible; the scenarios ship no food; and the two systems that could have produced some — hunting and
    the growing zones — were both dormant (no wild animal is ever spawned on a map, and nothing in src/ ever
    created a Zone_Growing). A settlement founded the ordinary way had literally nothing to eat, and its
    citizens went from 0.8 nutrition to zero in under a day and then beat each other to death in extreme
    mental breaks. This is the first link of that chain: something edible has to exist.

    nutrition 0.05 matches RimWorld's own RawBerries and this port's other raw foodstuffs (RawPotatoes,
    RawRice, Meat_Generic), so a cooking recipe measured in nutrition (IngredientValueGetter_Nutrition) needs
    no special case for it. preferability RawTasty is RimWorld's own for berries — better than RawBad raw
    produce, worse than any cooked meal — which is what keeps a citizen eating a meal first once there are
    meals. MarketValue is this port's own (RimWorld's is not sourceable here), placed between RawPotatoes
    (0.25) and Meat_Generic (0.4) rather than trusted as a literal.
  -->

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>RawBerries</defName>
    <label>berries</label>
    <description>Wild berries, picked by hand. Sweet, and gone almost as fast as they are gathered.</description>
    <category>Item</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Things.Thing</thingClass>
    <thingCategories><li>PlantFoodRaw</li></thingCategories>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <statBases><MarketValue>0.3</MarketValue></statBases>
    <ingestible>
      <nutrition>0.05</nutrition>
      <preferability>RawTasty</preferability>
      <foodType>VegetableOrFruit</foodType>
    </ingestible>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
